# The Preferences window's keys. An arrow key from this host goes to the focused box (which moves its cursor) and never reaches the window's
# own handler, so the window's Up and Down (the page before and after, round the six pages: Up from the first is the last, Down from the
# Map page the first) are called by the scene host's open step (prefs_key_up, prefs_key_down). A letter is ignored; Escape closes the window
# like Cancel and Return like OK (one option is turned over first, so that the words differ). The tab group is clicked after keys (a
# click keeps the page it leaves as the last page, a key does not). Return is the last step: the key also reaches the map, which opens
# the base screen, whose leader portraits animate slower than a snap (masked).
